      "extract": "[]{#sec:helons label=\"sec:helons\"} Let us now introduce our topologically-based toy model of quarks, leptons, and gauge bosons. It is convenient to represent the most fundamental objects in this model by twists through $\\pm\\pi$ in a ribbon. For convenience let us denote a twist through $\\pi$ as a \"dum\", and a twist through $-\\pi$ as a \"dee\" ($U$ and $E$ for short, after Tweedle-dum and Tweedle-dee [@wonderland]).",
